Mariusz "'''Loord'''" Cybulski {{born}} is a [[:Category:Poland|Polish]] professional ''[[Counter-Strike 2]]'' coach and a former professional ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive]]'' coach and player and ''[[Counter-Strike]]'' player.

In September 2020, '''Loord''' received a 6-month ban from all ESIC member events starting September 28, 2020 for exploiting a coach spectating bug during his time at [[Team Kinguin]] and [[Aristocracy]]. <ref>{{cite web|url=https://esic.gg/esports-integrity-commission-findings-from-investigation-into-csgo-spectator-bug-exploitation/|title=Esports Integrity Commission Findings from investigation into CS:GO Spectator Bug Exploitation|date=2020-09-28|publisher=[[ESIC]]}}</ref> Additionally, he received a five [[Majors|Major]] ban in January 2021 from [[Valve]] due to exploiting the coaching bug. <ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ESIC_Official/status/1354581403682304002|title=Today, Valve (@CSGO) ratified ESICs sanctions against coaches who exploited the Spectator Bug|date=2021-01-27|author=[[ESIC]]}}</ref>

He was part of the famous Polish player group [[Golden Five]], who were arguably one of the most successful teams in ''Counter-Strike'' history.

